  "headline_finding": "Stage 0 hard gate passed exactly. Positive control 1 (subgroup) returned exactly N/h-1 on every arm, both runs; positive control 2 (coset-union) matched its closed-form spectrum to ~1e-15. L2 at m=2 in-band on all 32 cells, both runs, no exceptions. A reproducible ABOVE-BAND signal was found specific to the j=0 curve at F=N/2 for L2/L3 at m=3,4, present in both independent seeds against a stable null population -- escalated per the contract's own falsification_criterion(d), not adjudicated by the Executor. All other above-band cells occurred only at small F where the null-vs-null control was itself noise-dominated across seeds. Stage 1 found KN-FIND-007's conservation mean is the multiset (not ordered) convention -- a non-contradictory distinct identity, not a stopping-rule trigger -- and found a previously undisclosed corpus inconsistency: KN-FIND-4c9e71's own later correction section reverses an 'O(1) max-C' verdict without either citing decision record (DEC-20260804-0a4bc2/-4f3a3b) being updated. Two of the four alpha values named in the hypothesis (0.0620, 0.0624) were not located in the corpus.",
